.TH TOUCH 1 "September 19, 2026" maux
.SH NAME
touch \- update date last modified of files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B touch
.RB [ \-t " stamp" | \-r " reference" ]
.I file ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Touch
attempts to set the modified date of each file.
If a file does not exist, an attempt will be made to create it.
New files have ProDOS TXT type; existing contents and other attributes
are left alone.
.TP
.B \-t stamp
Use [[CC]YY]MMDDhhmm[.SS]. The century is consumed but not stored;
seconds are parsed but discarded. Without a year, use the clock's year.
.TP
.B \-r reference
Copy the reference file's modification date and time.
.PP
Without either option, use the current ProDOS clock words.
If no clock is present this stores the honest ProDOS 'no date' value;
it is not an error.
.SH FILES
/usr/man/TOUCH  this page
.SH "SEE ALSO"
date(1), make(1), licenses(1)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Exit status is 0 if every file succeeds, 1 for file failures, 2 for usage or invalid stamp errors.
.SH BUGS
No -c, -a or -m options are implemented. Time has minute resolution; a century cannot be represented in the legacy date word.
